<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziri ibn Atiyya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1001</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziri ibn Atiyya was a chief of the Maghrawa, a Zenata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribe, and an ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>. Around 987 he took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> as Córdoba's governor, and in 994 he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oujda">Oujda</a>. He later broke with the regent al-Mansur, who drove him out of Fez, and he died in 1001, but his son al-Mu'izz was restored to Fez.</p></div>
